      "content": "body-armor for foot-soldiers made of iron rings or small thin iron plates sewn onto canvas, linen or leather and covered with a similar material. Originally in pairs (front and back), ergo often in the plural (OED s.v. brigandine) | body-armor for foot soldiers (OED s.v. brigander1)"
    }
